WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.370 --> 00:00:03.190
- I've been thinking about
this concept for a long time,

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.940
which is everybody who's driving right now

00:00:04.940 --> 00:00:06.870
who wants to build a huge business,

00:00:06.870 --> 00:00:11.130
I don't think really thinks
that kindness and empathy

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:15.890
and compassion and patience
are core to building an empire.

00:00:15.890 --> 00:00:18.210
And I thought I was the guy to write it

00:00:18.210 --> 00:00:19.980
because so much of what I've built

00:00:19.980 --> 00:00:22.470
and what I'm going to
build is based on things

00:00:22.470 --> 00:00:24.930
that your grandma would say you should do.

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:26.740
And I don't think that's
what people think about

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:28.540
when they're gonna build
a $100 million company.

00:00:28.540 --> 00:00:31.960
They think sharp elbows,
I'm gonna out negotiate.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:33.479
They think sports.
- Yeah

00:00:33.479 --> 00:00:37.260
And I think what sportsmen
and women do after a game

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:39.000
where they hug and they talk

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.830
and, you know, as a fan, I get upset

00:00:40.830 --> 00:00:43.280
when they Jets lose an
American football game

00:00:43.280 --> 00:00:44.750
and then are hugging and hanging out

00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:46.567
with the opponents after, I get mad.

00:00:46.567 --> 00:00:47.879
(everyone laughing)

00:00:47.879 --> 00:00:48.827
- [Kris] What are you doing!
- Correct.

00:00:48.827 --> 00:00:50.670
But that's exactly what
I think is required

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:52.360
of building a big business

00:00:52.360 --> 00:00:54.042
and I thought I was the guy to write it.

00:00:54.042 --> 00:00:55.680
- [Kris] We hear this word NFT.

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:56.890
- Yes.

00:00:56.890 --> 00:00:58.230
- [Kris] We think we understand it

00:00:58.230 --> 00:01:01.240
or some of us have absolutely no idea.

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:04.190
- Or a big part of people think
it's a scam and it's a fad.

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:07.250
- And it's coming up on
influencer's social media sites

00:01:07.250 --> 00:01:08.900
and you're like, well, I'm
not gonna get into this,

00:01:08.900 --> 00:01:11.183
people will laugh, Oh, you're doing NFTs.

00:01:12.600 --> 00:01:15.610
You have really shown the world

00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:18.770
and you've pioneered it in
your platform of 9 million,

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.420
just on Instagram alone

00:01:20.420 --> 00:01:23.810
of what NFTs can do and
how they can operate.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:25.896
Can you explain to someone right now

00:01:25.896 --> 00:01:27.940
and I know you've been
asked this question before,

00:01:27.940 --> 00:01:32.260
explain in basic terms, what an NFT is?

00:01:32.260 --> 00:01:35.730
- It's, let me say this
before I answer that question.

00:01:35.730 --> 00:01:37.100
Everybody who's listening right now

00:01:37.100 --> 00:01:39.270
is going to struggle with the concept

00:01:39.270 --> 00:01:41.840
because they're bringing
their internet brain

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:43.590
to the blockchain.

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.610
Let me say that one more time.

00:01:45.610 --> 00:01:47.930
The blockchain is such
a different platform

00:01:47.930 --> 00:01:51.150
than the internet, that when I
tell you that what an NFT is,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:54.220
is it's a digital asset that you own.

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.990
Most people don't understand
that because they're like,

00:01:55.990 --> 00:01:57.280
well, that doesn't work on the internet,

00:01:57.280 --> 00:01:59.490
I can right click and save the image.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:00.340
- [Kris] Sure.

00:02:00.340 --> 00:02:04.190
- So, the same way that in
1994, 95, 96, when I told people

00:02:04.190 --> 00:02:06.280
that people would buy wine on the internet

00:02:06.280 --> 00:02:08.900
and everybody who was 20, 30, 40, 50,

00:02:08.900 --> 00:02:10.950
thought that was stupid.

00:02:10.950 --> 00:02:13.520
Most people who think NFTs are stupid,

00:02:13.520 --> 00:02:15.050
don't realize that they've become

00:02:15.050 --> 00:02:17.240
their mom and dad and grandparents.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:19.060
Just like they thought
the internet was stupid,

00:02:19.060 --> 00:02:20.970
email was stupid, the iPhone was stupid,

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:23.890
social media was stupid,
online dating was stupid.

00:02:23.890 --> 00:02:27.270
People don't realize that
they are missing the boat

00:02:27.270 --> 00:02:28.103
on this technology.

00:02:28.103 --> 00:02:29.360
But the answer to your question is,

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.490
an NFT is a non fungible token

00:02:31.490 --> 00:02:34.680
which is a digital asset
that you actually own.

00:02:34.680 --> 00:02:35.710
And when people say,

00:02:35.710 --> 00:02:37.910
well, why would I wanna
own something digitally?

00:02:37.910 --> 00:02:38.749
I'd need to hold it.

00:02:38.749 --> 00:02:40.810
Well, a lot of people
who are driving right now

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.930
want a blue check mark on
their Instagram account,

00:02:42.930 --> 00:02:44.740
and guess what? You don't hold that.

00:02:44.740 --> 00:02:46.880
A lot of people want 10 million
followers on social media,

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.050
you don't hold that.

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:49.330
A lot of people live their life

00:02:49.330 --> 00:02:51.140
to take photos on the internet,

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.840
you don't hold that.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:54.300
We are living a digital life.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.900
And if you have children that
are buying skins on Fortnite.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.390
- [Kris] I've my both my
kids love buying skins.

00:02:59.390 --> 00:03:01.450
- Well, guess what?
That's a digital asset.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.160
And as we go more digital,

00:03:03.160 --> 00:03:06.410
your clout, your status,
your need to communicate

00:03:06.410 --> 00:03:07.740
is happening more digitally

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:09.410
than it's happening in real life.

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:13.050
People do things just for
a photo on social media.

00:03:13.050 --> 00:03:14.452
It's human psychology.

00:03:14.452 --> 00:03:17.740
Last of all, it's a smart contract.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:18.930
Meaning, the digital asset

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:21.130
can also mean something on the back end.

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:23.500
So for example, I have a
huge business conference

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.050
in Minnesota in May, called VeeCon.

00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:29.670
It's like a south by Southwests
Coachella of business.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:31.160
And the only way you can get in

00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:33.583
is if you own a VeeFriend,
it is the ticket.

00:03:33.583 --> 00:03:36.040
- [Kris] You're also opening up

00:03:36.040 --> 00:03:38.930
the first NFT restaurant in the world?

00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:39.763
- That's right.

00:03:39.763 --> 00:03:41.140
Fly Fish Club, which will open next year,

00:03:41.140 --> 00:03:42.580
early next year in New York City.

00:03:42.580 --> 00:03:43.890
- [Kris] Can I get membership?

00:03:43.890 --> 00:03:44.884
- If you buy it.

00:03:44.884 --> 00:03:47.265
(everyone laughing)

00:03:47.265 --> 00:03:48.098
- [Kris] That's why he's so rich.

00:03:48.098 --> 00:03:49.040
- But it's super interesting,

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.300
it's super interesting.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:53.180
A lot of people right now,
especially in this town,

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:54.870
they pay for a membership,

00:03:54.870 --> 00:03:57.660
country clubs, Soho
house, all these things,

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.870
but you pay, you don't own an asset.

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:03.400
With NFTs, your membership is an NFT,

00:04:03.400 --> 00:04:05.110
but if you decide after three months,

00:04:05.110 --> 00:04:06.440
you don't want to come anymore.

00:04:06.440 --> 00:04:08.740
You put it on a blockchain
and you sell it.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:12.950
It's creating a world where
your access or your membership

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:15.861
becomes an asset, not an expense.

00:04:15.861 --> 00:04:16.694
- [Kris] I understand that.

00:04:16.694 --> 00:04:17.610
- So think about that.

00:04:17.610 --> 00:04:19.629
- [Kris] So the NFT restaurant
that you're opening up,

00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:21.820
it's not a physical restaurant?

00:04:21.820 --> 00:04:22.950
- Oh, it's a physical restaurant.

00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:24.060
- [Kris] I'll be able to walk
into this thing if I want.

00:04:24.060 --> 00:04:25.500
- Yeah, this is not the metaverse,

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.800
which I think is much further
away than people think.

00:04:27.800 --> 00:04:29.390
I don't think we're living in VR.

00:04:29.390 --> 00:04:32.930
And people mix Metaverse and
NFT, they're separate things.

00:04:32.930 --> 00:04:35.180
This is a physical restaurant

00:04:35.180 --> 00:04:37.380
that is gonna be wildly premium,

00:04:37.380 --> 00:04:39.820
large location, highly in demand

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:42.840
that the NFT is just your membership.

00:04:42.840 --> 00:04:45.440
And so, that will open in Q1 of next year.

00:04:45.440 --> 00:04:46.450
- [Kris] Can't wait for it.

00:04:46.450 --> 00:04:48.798
Gary Vee in the studio, once again,

00:04:48.798 --> 00:04:49.798
