- Well, what about a marker?

00:18:35.240 --> 00:18:36.253
Like, a Sharpie.

00:18:37.120 --> 00:18:38.940
- [Priti] Why don't you make a doodle?

00:18:38.940 --> 00:18:40.801
- That's worth a million dollars.

00:18:40.801 --> 00:18:41.634
(everyone laughing)

00:18:41.634 --> 00:18:42.510
I don't know if you've heard,

00:18:42.510 --> 00:18:45.240
but I'm a pretty big artist now.

00:18:45.240 --> 00:18:46.450
My stuff sells at Christie's.

00:18:46.450 --> 00:18:49.470
- [Kris] Okay, so, what we'll do,

00:18:49.470 --> 00:18:50.850
why don't we lock in,

00:18:50.850 --> 00:18:52.730
can we take the hour, are
you being serious like this?

00:18:52.730 --> 00:18:56.190
- I'm being dead serious.
That's how much I love you.

00:18:56.190 --> 00:18:57.710
I'm absolutely happy to do it.

00:18:57.710 --> 00:18:59.110
- [Maz] An hour.

00:18:59.110 --> 00:19:02.530
- An hour Zoom in my time
before the end of the year,

00:19:02.530 --> 00:19:04.490
likely, June, July, August.

00:19:04.490 --> 00:19:05.430
I'm in.

00:19:05.430 --> 00:19:06.776
- [James] Well, this is nice.

00:19:06.776 --> 00:19:08.980
- Now, to give you a preview
of what just happened,

00:19:08.980 --> 00:19:12.130
in six months, Maha's
gonna email me and say,

00:19:12.130 --> 00:19:13.780
look, you gotta do that
hour, do you remember?

00:19:13.780 --> 00:19:17.260
And I'm gonna be very upset
that I committed to this.

00:19:17.260 --> 00:19:18.093
- [Kris] You are.

00:19:18.093 --> 00:19:20.240
- But now I'm stuck.
It's on public record.

00:19:20.240 --> 00:19:21.073
I'm in.

00:19:21.073 --> 00:19:21.906
- [Kris] All right.

00:19:21.906 --> 00:19:22.739
- [Maz] Are we taking the hour?

00:19:22.739 --> 00:19:24.609
- [Kris] We're taking Gary
Vee's hour. Thank you.

00:19:24.609 --> 00:19:26.500
(everyone clapping)

00:19:26.500 --> 00:19:28.070
- Now, you understand, we're in Dubai,

00:19:28.070 --> 00:19:29.470
by the way, we're in Dubai.

00:19:29.470 --> 00:19:31.379
I don't know who listens to this show,

00:19:31.379 --> 00:19:33.290
like, you might get offered
a private jet just for that.

00:19:33.290 --> 00:19:34.410
You might be done here.

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:36.380
- [Kris] Yeah, this is good. Thank you.

00:19:36.380 --> 00:19:37.460
- You're very, you should,

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:38.293
everybody who's listening,

00:19:38.293 --> 00:19:39.560
you should see his face right now.

00:19:39.560 --> 00:19:40.920
Kris is very excited.

00:19:40.920 --> 00:19:43.001
- [Kris] I'm gratituding.

00:19:43.001 --> 00:19:44.040
(laughs)

00:19:44.040 --> 00:19:45.950
I'm out of accountability of this.

00:19:45.950 --> 00:19:47.610
I'm going through everything
in your book right now.

00:19:47.610 --> 00:19:50.116
- [James] The best thing is
we get to keep our books.

00:19:50.116 --> 00:19:51.210
(laughs)

00:19:51.210 --> 00:19:52.150
- [Kris] So what we're gonna do,

00:19:52.150 --> 00:19:55.420
we're gonna bank that hour with
Gary Vee, we will bank that.

00:19:55.420 --> 00:19:57.130
We will officially kick off

00:19:57.130 --> 00:19:59.480
the Kris Fade Show Swap Meet tomorrow

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:02.230
with our first product
or our first object.

00:20:02.230 --> 00:20:03.930
Who knows what it's going to be.

00:20:03.930 --> 00:20:04.763
- [James] Oh, my God.

00:20:04.763 --> 00:20:07.283
- [Kris] Gary Vee, we love you, man.

00:20:07.283 --> 00:20:08.116
- I love you back.

00:20:08.116 --> 00:20:09.290
- [Kris] Thank you so much
for coming in as usual.

00:20:09.290 --> 00:20:10.123
- Thanks for having me.

00:20:10.123 --> 00:20:11.557
- [Kris] Go and grab the book.

00:20:11.557 --> 00:20:14.250
"Twelve and a Half: Leveraging
the Emotional Ingredients

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:16.525
Necessary for Business Success".

00:20:16.525 --> 00:20:19.525
(everyone clapping)

00:20:21.433 --> 00:20:24.016
(upbeat music)

